    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>
      The mission of the Urdaneta City Public Library is to be an inclusive center for knowledge, learning, and cultural
      enrichment. Provide equal access to diverse resources, services, and programs that promote intellectual growth
      through digital innovation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Offer user-friendly digital platforms, virtual programs, online resources, and accessible e-government services
      to meet community needs—creating an inclusive and welcoming space that nurtures curiosity, fosters lifelong
      learning, and empowers individuals to thrive in a changing world.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <span class="card-icon">🌟</span>
    <h2>Vision</h2>
    <p>
      Urdaneta City Library envisions itself to be Pangasinan&apos;s prime source of quality information services and the
      center for educational technology in the community:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Acquire a more extensive and a well-balanced collection of books, magazines, electronic resources, and other library materials.</li>
      <li>Enhance research techniques through automated access to sophisticated tools such as electronic and online resources.</li>
      <li>Learn community needs through community study and design services that are responsive to those needs.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
